<question type="multichoice">
  <name>
    <text>NEET_UG_PHYSICS_MCQ_Q05 - Distance covered by particle in first four seconds</text>
  </name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The displacement of a particle is given by \(x = (t - 2)^2\) where \(x\) is in metres and \(t\) in seconds. The distance covered by the particle in first 4 seconds is</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The position function is \(x(t) = (t - 2)^2\), with position \(x\) in metres and time \(t\) in seconds. The interval of interest is from \(t = 0\text{ s}\) to \(t = 4\text{ s}\).</p><p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>Motion takes place in one dimension along the \(x\)-axis. Distance is the total path length traversed, which accumulates regardless of the direction of motion, while displacement is the net difference between final and initial positions.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>- Instantaneous velocity:\[ v(t) = \frac{dx}{dt} \]- A turning point occurs where \(v(t) = 0\).<br/>- Total distance is calculated by summing the absolute path lengths traveled across each monotonic segment between turning points.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>- Differentiating position with respect to time:\[ v(t) = \frac{d}{dt}\left[(t - 2)^2\right] = 2(t - 2)\text{ m/s} \]- Setting velocity to zero to identify turning points:\[ 2(t - 2) = 0 \implies t = 2\text{ s} \]Since \(t = 2\text{ s}\) lies within \([0, 4\text{ s}]\), the particle changes its direction of motion at \(t = 2\text{ s}\).<br/>- Finding positions at boundaries and the turning point:<ul><li>At \(t = 0\text{ s}\): \(x(0) = (0 - 2)^2 = 4\text{ m}\)</li><li>At \(t = 2\text{ s}\): \(x(2) = (2 - 2)^2 = 0\text{ m}\)</li><li>At \(t = 4\text{ s}\): \(x(4) = (4 - 2)^2 = 4\text{ m}\)</li></ul>- Distance traveled during \(t = 0\text{ s}\) to \(t = 2\text{ s}\):\[ s_1 = |x(2) - x(0)| = |0 - 4| = 4\text{ m} \]- Distance traveled during \(t = 2\text{ s}\) to \(t = 4\text{ s}\):\[ s_2 = |x(4) - x(2)| = |4 - 0| = 4\text{ m} \]- Total distance covered in the first 4 seconds:\[ s = s_1 + s_2 = 4\text{ m} + 4\text{ m} = 8\text{ m} \]</p><p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>The net displacement over 4 seconds is \(x(4) - x(0) = 4 - 4 = 0\text{ m}\), but accounting for the reversal of direction at \(t = 2\text{ s}\) yields a total path length of \(8\text{ m}\).<br/>The distance covered by the particle in the first 4 seconds is \(8\text{ m}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
